<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A channel can agree to do something at a time — a tournament, a film night, a meeting — and everyone sees it, says whether they are coming, and is reminded shortly before it starts."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_clock}>{dgettext("help_features", "Scheduling One")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Operators only, with /event followed by how long from now it starts and what it is called: /event 2h Tuesday tournament. The time is a delay rather than a clock reading, so it means the same instant for everybody who can read it, wherever they are."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_group_view}>{dgettext("help_features", "Your Own Clock")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The card shows the start in your own time zone, and how far off it is. Two people in different countries see different clock times for the same event, which is the point: the stored instant is the same one."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_checkmark}>
  {dgettext("help_features", "Saying You Will Be There")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Press I'm going on the card. It is the only answer there is — a maybe tells the organiser nothing they did not already know. Press it again to take yourself back off. The count beside it is everybody who said yes."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_megaphone}>{dgettext("help_features", "The Reminder")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Shortly before it starts, the channel gets a line saying so, and everyone who said they were going gets a notification — a desktop one if you have the chat open, a push one if you do not. There is no separate alerts channel and no setting of its own: it uses the notifications you have already chosen."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_channel_list}>
  {dgettext("help_features", "The Events Window")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Start ▸ Tools ▸ Events, or /event with nothing after it, lists what this channel has coming up, soonest first. Whoever scheduled something can call it off with /event cancel followed by its number; the record that it was going to happen stays."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-event">
    {dgettext("help_features", "/event")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-desktop-notifications">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Desktop Notifications")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-closed-app-notifications">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Notifications When the App Is Closed")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
